  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add `chunk_topk_distill_function` — a chunked fused-linear top-k forward-KL kernel that lets a downstream verl VeOmni engine compute distillation loss **without materializing the `[T, V]` student logits tensor**. Rides the same chunked autograd pattern as `chunk_logprobs.py`; reuses its per-token NLL / entropy helpers to keep bitwise-vs-verl on the shared outputs.\n- Route `return_log_probs=True` + `teacher_topk_ids` + `teacher_topk_log_probs` (+ optional `log_prob_min_clamp`) through `ForCausalLMLoss` / `_chunk_loss_dispatch` to the new kernel. Loss wrappers now return a uniform 7-tuple `(loss, logits, log_probs, entropy, distillation_losses, student_mass, teacher_mass)`; non-distill paths fill trailing slots with `None`.\n- Add `distillation_losses` / `student_mass` / `teacher_mass` (`Optional[Tensor]`, fp32, `labels` shape) to `CausalLMOutputWithLogProbs`, `MoeCausalLMOutputWithLogProbs`, and all per-model subclasses (Qwen2-VL, Qwen2.5-VL, Qwen3-VL, Qwen3-VL-MoE, Qwen2.5-Omni, Qwen3-Omni-MoE). `student_mass` / `teacher_mass` are detached (metrics-only, matching verl's contract).\n- Update every per-model patchgen config to unpack the 7-tuple and thread the three new fields into the output dataclass. Inline output-dataclass declarations (`add_helper_after`) also extended. Regenerated all 22 modeling files via `make patchgen`.\n\n## What verl needs\n\nTwo additive patches documented in `docs/design/verl_topk_distill_integration.md` — both symmetric with the existing `output.log_probs` / `output.entropy` handling, no impact on the non-fused path:\n\n1. `verl/workers/engine/veomni/transformer_impl.py:prepare_model_inputs` — thread teacher tensors into `model_inputs` when `distillation_use_topk=True` (~15 lines).\n2. `verl/workers/engine/fsdp/transformer_impl.py:prepare_model_outputs` — extend the `use_fused_kernels=True` arm to read the three new fields off `output` and wrap as nested tensors (~15 lines).\n\nNo changes to `compute_forward_kl_topk`, `distillation_ppo_loss`, `DistillationConfig`, micro-batch fields, or estimator-only loss modes (k1/k2/k3/kl/...).\n\n## Numerics\n\nKernel forward-KL formula is verbatim verl's `kl_divergence(log_q, log_p) = (exp(log_p) * (log_p - log_q)).sum(-1)` on the teacher's top-k support. Backward is closed-form: three additive `dlogits` contributions (log_probs / entropy / topk-KL) matmul-folded to `(dhidden, dweight)`, identical dtype/temperature op order to `chunk_logprobs.py` so the bitwise-vs-verl story carries over on the shared outputs.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pytest tests/ops/test_chunk_topk_distill.py` — 9 passed locally, 1 skipped (`verl` import — `ray` not in venv). On H100 worker: 9 passed + 1 skipped.\n- [x] `pytest tests/ops/test_chunk_logprobs.py` (regression) — 7 passed + 3 skipped (verl-equivalence subcases gated on same `ray` import). On H100: 7 passed + 3 skipped.\n- [x] `pytest tests/models/test_return_log_probs_e2e.py` — 8/8 pass on H100, including the new `test_return_log_probs_with_topk_distill_populates_three_fields` parametrized over `qwen3-text` and `qwen3_vl-vlm`. Asserts: three new fields populated, `distillation_losses ≥ 0`, `student_mass`/`teacher_mass ∈ [0, 1]`, mass tensors detached, **bitwise-equal to the kernel called directly on `model.lm_head.weight`**, backward through `distillation_losses` reaches `lm_head.weight.grad`.\n- [x] `make patchgen && git diff` — only the expected per-model unpack + output-dataclass changes (plus a small amount of pre-existing patchgen formatting drift against current HF v5.2.0).\n- [x] `make quality` clean.\n- [ ] Verl-side dry run once the two integration patches land in a verl branch.\n\n## File-by-file\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `veomni/ops/kernels/cross_entropy/chunk_topk_distill.py` | **new** kernel (`_ChunkedLinearTopkDistill` autograd Function + wrapper) |\n| `veomni/ops/kernels/cross_entropy/__init__.py` | dispatch branch + 7-tuple return shape |\n| `veomni/utils/model_outputs.py` | three new fields × 8 dataclasses |\n| `veomni/models/transformers/*/*_patch_gen_config.py` | per-model unpack + output-dataclass extensions (17 configs) |\n| `veomni/models/transformers/*/generated/*.py` | `make patchgen` regenerated (do not hand-edit) |\n| `tests/ops/test_chunk_topk_distill.py` | **new** kernel tests (correctness + closed-form backward + clamp + IGN masking + verl equivalence) |\n| `tests/models/test_return_log_probs_e2e.py` | **new** e2e contract test on `qwen3` and `qwen3_vl` |\n| `docs/design/verl_topk_distill_integration.md` | **new** integration guide with the exact two verl-side patches |",
